--- SECTION 8/9/10: NEURAL NETWORK (Dropout 0.3, Early Stopping) ---
Architecture:
  Input (scaled/encoded features)
  -> Dense(64, relu)   : learns 64 weighted combinations of features
  -> Dropout(0.3)      : randomly silences 30% of neurons each step
  -> Dense(32, relu)   : a smaller second layer refines the patterns
  -> Dense(1, sigmoid) : squashes output to a churn probability [0,1]

EARLY STOPPING REPORT:
Training was stopped at epoch 14 because validation loss stopped improving (best epoch = 6, patience = 8).
Neural Network (Dropout 0.3) TEST metrics: {'accuracy': 0.7896, 'precision': 0.6343, 'recall': 0.4893, 'f1': 0.5524}

--- SECTION 11: BIAS / VARIANCE DEMO ---
Main model — train accuracy: 0.8119, val accuracy: 0.8180, gap: -0.0061
Small gap  -> balanced bias/variance (good fit).
Big gap    -> high variance (overfitting).

Underfitting model (1 neuron) — train acc 0.8064, val acc 0.8218, val F1 0.6342
Both plateau at the same level with ~0 gap -> HIGH BIAS
(too simple to capture more of the signal).
Oversized model (no reg., 150 epochs) — train acc 0.9667, val acc 0.7507, gap 0.2160
Main model (dropout + early stopping) — train acc 0.8119, val acc 0.8180, gap -0.0061
The oversized model memorizes the training set: the large train/val
gap is the fingerprint of HIGH VARIANCE (overfitting).

--- SECTION 12: 5-FOLD CROSS-VALIDATION ---
Methodology: the TRAINING set is split into 5 folds. For each fold,
the scaler is refit on the 4 training folds only (no leakage) and
the NN is trained with early stopping using the held-out fold.
The TEST set is never touched here.
Fold 1: accuracy=0.7990 precision=0.6600 recall=0.5038 f1=0.5714
