--- SECTION 19: CONCLUSIONS ---
1. Best model by F1          : Logistic Regression (F1=0.5692)
2. Dataset imbalanced        : Yes (~26.5% churn)
3. Accuracy misleading?      : Yes — a dummy 'always stay' model would reach ~73% accuracy.
4. Overfitting observed?     : Yes — oversized unregularized model gap +0.216 vs main model gap -0.006
5. Dropout effect            : F1 0.5196 -> 0.5524
6. L1 effect                 : F1 0.5524 -> 0.5109
7. L2 effect                 : F1 0.5524 -> 0.5477
8. Best regularization       : Dropout
9. CV said about variance    : F1 = 0.571 +/- 0.021
10. Early stopping epoch     : stopped at 14, best = 6
11. Why that epoch           : val loss did not improve for 8 epochs
12. NN vs baseline           : logistic F1 0.5692 vs NN F1 0.5524
13. Top churn drivers        : tenure, Contract_Two year, TotalCharges, Contract_Month-to-month, InternetService_DSL
14. Limitations              : small dataset, single split for final
                               evaluation, no class-weight tuning,
                               no hyperparameter search.

All results saved to results.json and figures to ./figures/
